pack operator-financial-membrane
generation control-1
provenance binding the compute ledger to the autonomous operator, 2026-08-27
authority measured
note Continues compute-financial-metabolism and compute-governance-closed. Nothing from those is superseded; this connects them to the thing that was actually spending. The operator is the largest consumer in the estate and it had no funding awareness at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE OPERATOR IS BURNING RIGHT NOW
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim clm:operator-live-retry-storm
  status UNRESOLVED
  verification MEASURED
  claim The autonomous operator is failing continuously, at the time of writing, and reports itself paused while doing so.
  evidence 3,574 runs recorded; run count observed incrementing by 1 every 25-30 seconds during measurement
  evidence newest three runs at 20:37:53, 20:38:22, 20:38:51 all RateLimitError 429
  evidence mcp operator_status reports paused=true; launchd com.bonfyre.agents-runtime PID 28220 is alive and dispatching
  consequence the pause control is not honoured by the runtime, so the documented way to stop it does not stop it
  cost_qualifier these requests are REJECTED for insufficient quota, so they cost no money; the waste is CPU, disk and 4.8 hours of run time, not dollars
  action_required either the runtime must honour the pause flag, or the launchd job must be unloaded to stop it
  stop_command launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bonfyre.agents-runtime.plist

claim clm:operator-failure-taxonomy
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim Three failure modes account for every operator failure, and only one is still live.
  total 3,530 failed runs of 3,557; exactly 4 have ever resolved
  mode_1 1,923 ValidationError on InputTokensDetails.cache_write_tokens, 2026-07-27 to 2026-08-23 -- RESOLVED
  mode_2 1,367+ credit_balance_exhausted, 2026-08-27 01:00 onward -- LIVE
  mode_3 225 connection errors
  note mode_1 was the largest historical failure mode and was cleared by the vendored default added 2026-08-26 22:41; every validation failure predates that patch, which is how the fix is known to have worked

upgrade upg:beta-response-usage-patched
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  target ~/.bonfyre/agents-runtime/venv/.../openai/types/beta/beta_response_usage.py
  change cache_write_tokens defaulted to 0, mirroring the earlier patch to responses/response_usage.py
  cause the same latent bug existed on the beta path with no default; responses/ was patched 2026-08-26, beta/ was not
  verified both InputTokensDetails classes now construct with cached_tokens only and yield cache_write_tokens=0
  caveat vendored-dependency edit; does not survive a venv rebuild. Backup at scratchpad/beta_response_usage.py.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE GUARD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

upgrade upg:funding-preflight
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  claim A preflight consulted once refuses every run the operator attempted 1,380 times.
  mechanism provider-scoped funding route lookup, then a TTL-cached provider balance check
  organs financial_metabolism funding_routes; the balance surfaces already probed for the ledger
  result openrouter $0.05 REFUSE (no route), openai $0.05 ADMIT, anthropic $5 ADMIT, anthropic $500 REFUSE (route holds $300)
  replay 1,380 runs would have been refused before dispatch; 1,380 provider requests avoided
  cost the guard itself is capped at 288 requests/day by a 300s balance cache
  boundary the operator is NOT modified; the guard is offered, wiring it in is a separate decision

defect def:choose-funding-is-not-provider-scoped
  status OPEN
  verification REPRODUCED
  target financial_metabolism.choose_funding
  symptom choose_funding(currency, amount) selects any active route with sufficient balance, so an OpenRouter request was funded by route:compute/anthropic
  effect a provider whose own budget is exhausted is admitted against another provider's pocket
  workaround the guard queries funding_routes directly with a provider-scoped route_id prefix
  fix_shape an optional provider or subject filter on choose_funding

defect def:my-own-guard-skipped-the-overdrawn-case
  status FIXED
  verification REPRODUCED
  claim The first version of the guard admitted the exact case it was written to refuse.
  symptom the balance test read `bal >= 0 and bal < estimate`, which skips the refusal precisely when the balance is NEGATIVE, i.e. overdrawn
  detected the replay reported 0 runs prevented against 1,380 that plainly should have been
  fix a non-positive balance now always refuses, and the -1 sentinel for "reachable but unknown" is handled separately
  note the replay measurement is what caught it; a guard that is never replayed against real history is not known to guard anything

